M — Match

This is a hashing / dictionary lookup problem.

Brute force would compare every pair:

Time: O(n²)
Space: O(1)

With a dictionary, for each number we ask:

“Have I already seen the number I need to reach target?”

Dictionary lookup is average O(1), so one pass gives O(n).

P — Plan

For each nums[i]:

Calculate the complement:
second_num = target - nums[i]
Check whether second_num is already in dic.
If yes, return the stored index and current index.
Otherwise, store nums[i]: i.

An important detail is that we check before inserting the current number. This prevents using the same element twice.

I — Implement
class Solution:
    def twoSum(self, nums: List[int], target: int) -> List[int]:
        dic = {}


        for i in range(len(nums)):
            second_num = target - nums[i]


            if second_num in dic:
                return [dic[second_num], i]


            dic[nums[i]] = i

